---
title: "Stepper"
description: "Astro tag-components (Stepper/Step/StepperFinished) rendered as static HTML, with a headless Preact controller (client:load) driving accordion navigation, expand/collapse, and localStorage progress."
type: interactive
---

A step-by-step guide. Steps render as static HTML at build time; a small Preact controller wires up navigation, an expand/collapse-all toggle, and progress persistence on the existing DOM.

By default the stepper behaves as an accordion: only the active step's body is shown, and readers move through with **Next** / **Previous**, or by clicking a step title. Pass `open=true` to start with every step expanded.

## Properties

### `stepper` tag

| Property | Type      | Default | Description                                                        |
|----------|-----------|---------|--------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `open`   | `boolean` | `false` | When true, all steps start expanded instead of as an accordion.    |
| `level`  | `string`  | `h3`    | Heading level for step titles (`h1`–`h6`).                         |

### `step` tag (child of `stepper`)

| Property | Type     | Default | Description                          |
|----------|----------|---------|--------------------------------------|
| `title`  | `string` | —       | Required. The step's heading text.   |

### `stepper-finished` tag (child of `stepper`)

Optional. Its content is shown after the reader finishes the last step. No attributes.

## Examples

### Accordion (default)

{% stepper %}
{% step title="Install the Datadog Agent" %}
Download and install the Agent for your platform.

```shell
DD_API_KEY=<YOUR_API_KEY> bash -c "$(curl -L https://install.datadoghq.com/scripts/install_script_agent7.sh)"
```
{% /step %}
{% step title="Configure the integration" %}
Edit the configuration file and restart the Agent.
{% /step %}
{% step title="Verify data is flowing" %}
Check the integration status in the Datadog UI.
{% /step %}
{% stepper-finished %}
You're all set. Your data should now be flowing into Datadog.
{% /stepper-finished %}
{% /stepper %}

### Expanded (`open=true`)

{% stepper open=true %}
{% step title="First step" %}
This stepper starts fully expanded.
{% /step %}
{% step title="Second step" %}
All step bodies are visible at once.
{% /step %}
{% /stepper %}

### Single step

{% stepper %}
{% step title="The only step" %}
A single-step stepper renders no connecting line.
{% /step %}
{% /stepper %}

### Complex content (code blocks and tabs)

{% stepper %}

{% step title="Install the database" %}
Run the following command to install FakeDB:

```shell
curl -fsSL https://fakedb.example.com/install.sh | bash
```

After the installation completes, verify that FakeDB is running:

```shell
fakedb --version
```
{% /step %}

{% step title="Configure the database" %}

Create a configuration file for FakeDB:

{% tabs %}

{% tab label="YAML" %}
```yaml
fakedb:
  host: localhost
  port: 5432
  database: mydb
  username: admin
  password: secret
  max_connections: 100
  timeout: 30s
```
{% /tab %}

{% tab label="JSON" %}
```json
{
  "fakedb": {
    "host": "localhost",
    "port": 5432,
    "database": "mydb",
    "username": "admin",
    "password": "secret",
    "max_connections": 100,
    "timeout": "30s"
  }
}
```
{% /tab %}
{% /tabs %}

{% /step %}

{% step title="Connect to the database" %}
Start the FakeDB service and open a connection:

```shell
fakedb start
fakedb connect --host localhost --port 5432 --database mydb --username admin
```

To verify the connection is working, run a test query:

```shell
fakedb query "SELECT 1;"
```
{% /step %}

{% /stepper %}
